sequenceDiagram
  actor HUMAN as Maintainer
  participant PROJECT as GitHub Projects portfolio
  participant GH as GitHub event source
  participant APP as GitHub App installation
  participant CP as Agentic Delivery Control Plane
  participant ENROLL as Control Plane participant contract
  participant ORIGIN as Origin repository
  participant TYPES as Native Issue Type on issue
  participant DEFINITIONS as Organization issue-field definitions API
  participant VALUES as Per-issue field values API
  participant PR as Origin pull request
  participant VALIDATOR as Independent Validator
  participant EVAL as Versioned evaluation
  participant EVIDENCE as Delivery and outcome evidence

  HUMAN->>PROJECT: prioritize linked source Issue and track portfolio progress
  PROJECT-->>ORIGIN: reference only; a Project-only card is planning input
  Note over PROJECT,CP: Project membership, fields, status, and events never authorize execution
  GH->>APP: subscribed event for source Issue
  APP->>APP: apply installation access and deliver event
  APP->>CP: event envelope with repository ID
  CP->>ENROLL: check selected repository and exact participant pins
  Note over APP,ENROLL: App installation access and Control Plane enrollment are separate checks
  CP->>ORIGIN: re-fetch source Issue, repository identity, actor permission, and native Issue Type
  alt issue identity, access, or permission is missing
    CP-->>GH: hold; leave Issue and repository unchanged
  else source Issue is authorized
  CP->>DEFINITIONS: read organization field definitions and option IDs
  CP->>VALUES: read this issue's field values using repository permissions
  Note over TYPES,ORIGIN: Organization Issue Type definitions and an issue's native type value are related but distinct surfaces
  Note over TYPES,VALUES: Issue Type, lifecycle position, delivery authorization, governance metadata, and runner state remain distinct
  CP->>CP: interpret intent; propose route and field values
  CP->>CP: deterministically validate identity, permission, schema, option, transition, and orchestration contracts
  CP->>ORIGIN: mutate only the originating issue or bounded branch after gates pass
  ORIGIN->>PR: publish tested issue-linked change
  PR->>VALIDATOR: request independent semantic and provenance review
  VALIDATOR->>EVAL: run versioned offline evaluation and report result
  EVAL->>EVIDENCE: record dataset, grader, candidate pins, baseline, and result
  HUMAN->>PR: decide whether to merge
  HUMAN->>PROJECT: reprioritize an improvement Issue from reviewed evidence
  Note over PROJECT,PR: Human approval and merge remain outside agent authority
  CP->>VALUES: write only validated per-issue field values
  Note over CP,VALUES: Issue-value writes do not change organization definitions or Project-owned planning fields
  CP-->>GH: publish evidence and origin write-back links
  end
  Note over APP,CP: Webhook delivery replay restores event processing only
  Note over CP,ORIGIN: Codex session continuation restores one bounded runner operation only
  Note over EVAL,EVIDENCE: Evaluation replay repeats a versioned dataset and grader; it is not webhook or session replay
  Note over GH,ORIGIN: Target sequence; the 2026-09-24 live audit had no passing end-to-end run
  Note over PROJECT,CP: 2026-10-09 status: complete org/user Project inventory returned none and 19 open Issues had no associations; the latest observed run skipped delivery and proves no end-to-end flow
